k="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602636f1"/></fig><fig id="fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Number of genes methylated in the serum of gastric cancer patients and control.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602636f2"/></fig><fig id="fig3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Association between cancer staging and concentrations of methylated DNA. (<bold>A</bold>) <italic>APC</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.08); (<bold>B</bold>) <italic>E-cadherin</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.2); (<bold>C</bold>) <italic>TIMP3</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.005) and (<bold>D</bold>) <italic>hMLH1</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.03). The horizontal line indicated the median concentrations of the patients' subgroups.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602636f3"/></fig><fig id="fig4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Kaplan&#x02013;Meier analysis of the probability of overall survival in gastric cancer patients according to methylation status. (<bold>A</bold>) <italic>APC</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.20); (<bold>B</bold>) <italic>E-cadherin</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.09); (<bold>C</bold>) combined <italic>APC</italic> and <italic>E-cadherin</italic> (<italic>P</italic>=0.006).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="92-6602636f4"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Summary of primer sequences and probe used for quantitative MSP</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Marker</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Primer sequences</bold></th><th align="left" valign